  "live_records": {
    "q-358220": {
      "dom_id": "step-q358220",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}\\frac{9}{{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}\\frac{9}{{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}9{(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}9{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=3x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=3x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{9}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}9{\\int }_{\\pi /12}^{\\pi /9}{sec}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =9{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{tan}⁡u{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =3(\\sqrt{3}-1) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}-3.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
