    "q-114301": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114301",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot 2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot 2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
